<title>RUSSIA: Russian Jan-July oil output flat yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Russian Jan-July oil output flat yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian crude oil output in January-July totalled 172 million tonnes, a 0.5 percent rise on year-ago levels, State Statistics Committee figures released on Friday showed.</p>
<p>The committee released the following data for energy production:</p>
<p>			January-July 1997	July 1997 output:</p>
<p>		   in million     yr/yr	  pct change on</p>
<p>		     tonnes     pct change   July 1996</p>
<p>June 1997</p>
<p> Crude oil	172	     +0.5	   +0.7	 +3.2</p>
<p> Refined oil    103	     -1.3	   +2.6	 +2.6</p>
<p> Gasoline	  15.6	   -0.8	   +2.2	 +4.9</p>
<p> Diesel	    27.7	   -0.2	   +4.4	 +3.5</p>
<p>Heavy fuel oil</p>
<p>  (mazut)	  36.9	   -2.0	   +6.4	 +0.4</p>
<p> Lubricants	 1.2	  -13.6	   -6.5	 +6.1</p>
<p> Natural gas    318	     -6.3	  -14.8	 -4.6</p>
<p>(billion cubic metres)</p>
<p> Gas condensate   5.0	   +1.5	   +4.7	 -2.9</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
